vernment. The bill would amend the Homeland Security Act of 2002 with authority for the Secretary of the Department of Homeland Security to order the suspension or shutdown of AI systems. AI developers that refuse to shut systems down could face fines of up $20 million for each day on which a violation occurs. Read full article Commentsƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;p3lbtkm4hIu5E34Q9t9UygKMlaXOrGc_lP7JAWXBk6Eƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;K_Z2C17pVHa_-PSbmrAg6jRlC_aJOMZIG_J5vsDhn58ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;-n5ktdDOVynA4qeCMnlEoVKURkQSEcJJzZ_t4R-EKb0ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;AkMgh4DpceLT1h-2kG8WZRbcTSrtNJNDhLNH8YtiBgUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;bfnijzy8Nk2tBoYmp1x6ejLGolAVarEBXeNyRsea4YYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;5VtRDJKwdngIfU1rs0CAf14-WvHUlGJ1CZFaVF-Y3LYƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;lcIFjVy3-FZuv_dmmF1NKqfXPskv4gGs-MbJ_RwhsVkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkdTextƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;J_5USLnpL4nxQuH-n76K0M6Ome7C4vBfS1-ojqPuQXYƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkqSyndicationSourceƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;VPKn_dIjhF8yIXzTN1FqNO7R-2RIVge3fN-wFKDm7cUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx(urn:rmn:predicate:source-reports-